The evaluation model adopted is based on the form of Architecture Tradeoff Analysis Method (ATAM). It pinpoints the drivers of each quality attribute and assesses each and scores them based on these attributes, recording those trade-offs that each style entails [15]. This then becomes transparent and repeatable with a weighted decision matrix [1].
Weights are based on Section 2.2: high frequency consists of the band having produced the most and is the most unique driver with the remaining drivers considered equally important by being given an equal weight. The scores are the team's conclusions, verified and based upon the sources provided. A sensitivity check was performed by double the weight corresponding to operational simplicity to 40 % and scale the other weights accordingly. So the style that was nominated is still narrowly ahead (3.79 compared to 3.76 that the modular monolith achieved), meaning that the monolith is a good runner-up and the size of the team is all important.
